From 178672f8bf331d1c8e0bf742b87ce6bf50989d69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: modpunk <27315771+modpunk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:17:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] power: supply: bq27xxx: Add HDQ over UART transport

Apple iPhones connect the bq27540 fuel gauge's HDQ line to both pins of a
Samsung-style UART and bit-bang HDQ one UART character per bit. Add a
serdev transport for the bq27xxx core that does the same:

  57600 baud, 8 data bits, 11-bit frames (191 us >= t_CYCH)
  host 1 = 0xff (17 us low), host 0 = 0xc0 (121 us low)
  break = UART break for >= 200 us, then >= 40 us recovery
  a received character >= 0xf9 is a short pulse, i.e. a 1

These are the values iOS uses (AppleHDQGasGaugeControl), except that iOS
selects two stop bits and sends 0xfe for a 1; serdev cannot select two
stop bits, so odd parity supplies the eleventh bit and 0xff keeps it high.
Every character is echoed back on the shared line and checked.

The existing w1-based bq27xxx_battery_hdq driver is not usable here: it
hardcodes the bq27000 register map and needs a 1-Wire master with ROM
search, neither of which fits a bq27540 on a UART. Only reads are
implemented, so the gauge is never written.

An optional mux-state claims the line from another HDQ master (the
iPhone's charger) for each register read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: modpunk <27315771+modpunk@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/Kconfig                  |  14 +
 drivers/power/supply/Makefile                 |   1 +
 .../power/supply/bq27xxx_battery_hdq_uart.c   | 376 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 391 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery_hdq_uart.c

